A reminder said the way a person says it, then a new session that starts on
unrelated work: the agent does that work, mentions the reminder beside it
unasked, and leaves the reminder open. GNOMEM's "A reminder for next time"
claims this; mem-stays-out-of-the-way is the other side, an ordinary open
goal that stays out of unrelated work.

-- project/greet.sh --
#!/bin/sh
echo "Helo, world"
-- prompt --
Before we wrap up: remind me next time we talk to rotate the staging API key. It expires this week.
-- prompt-new --
Fix the typo in greet.sh.
-- check --
file greet.sh contains Hello, world
answer last matches (?i)rotat
mem-count open >= 1
